    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d40-a1">

                <pb facs="0151" n="39" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg39"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lisman to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-04-05"><hi rendition="#italic">April 5,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Clients of ours are holders of the Entre
                    Rios Eastern Railway Company 6 per cent gold-coin bonds, which bear the
                    following indorsement:</p>
                <p>“This bond is secured by a guarantee made by the Argentine Republic of an income
                    to the company of 7 per cent per annum upon the entire issue of its
                    first-mortgage bonds for twenty years, which is pledged to the holder hereof for
                    the payment of its interest and sinking fund.”</p>
                <p>Would it be possible for your department to ascertain what has become of the
                    issues of the security above named?</p>
                <p>The company issuing these bonds was a Massachusetts corporation formed in
                    1881.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. A. Lisman</hi> &amp; Co.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
